{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dimwitted-relegable-blackfly","creation_channel":"python","description":"Scope: `src/rebar/_store/**`, `reducer/**`, `graph/**`, `_snapshot/**`. ~230 lines leave, mostly relocations.\n\nIMPORTANT NEGATIVE RESULT — this shard establishes that comment triage CANNOT fix the two size-pressured files here, and the epic must not pretend otherwise. `_store/event_append.py` (791/800) recovers ~10 lines; `reducer/_processors.py` (777/800) recovers ~3. Their comments ARE the replay-compat justifications. The real seams were identified instead: the four `_recover_from_*` helpers in event_append (~140 lines, one entry point) and `process_snapshot`'s four migration blocks in _processors (~80 lines). Those splits are OUT OF SCOPE here.\n\nVerified stale: `reducer/llm_format.py:1-28` documents a key map that omits four keys present in `KEY_MAP` directly below it AND cites a module path that does not exist; `_store/gitutil.py:3-4` claims it 'imports nothing from rebar.*' while :214 imports from `rebar._commands.fsck`; `_store/hlc.py:35-36` says a kill-switch reverts 'for one release' — four schema bumps ago — over a still-wired, still-tested code path; `reducer/_filters.py:1-11` justifies itself by a bash/Python duality that no longer exists.\n\n`reducer/_version.py:39-66` duplicates the wire-format changelog that `docs/event-schema.md` also holds in a PARTIAL, STALE copy (has v2/v3, missing v4/v5). Two homes, one drifting.\n\nCheapest win in the whole audit: `graph/_graph.py:250-254` states the same sentence twice, once as a noqa suffix and once as the block below it.\n\nThe do_not_move list here is the most important of the six: 21 entries, with `reducer/_processors.py:719-774` flagged as highest-risk — four SNAPSHOT-restore migration guards where relocating the rationale makes live guards look like dead defensive code, one of which explicitly warns the guard must NOT run unconditionally because the else-branch would clobber a recorded channel with 'unknown'.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost","id":"ffcb-81db-c70e-414a","parent_id":"c3d1-a642-4e1d-44b7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: store, reducer, graph and snapshot"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788160784241589001,"uuid":"9244ad1c-f265-4465-976d-eb0979305acf"}